<title>UK: TABLE - TLG profits decline in year.</title>
<headline>TABLE - TLG profits decline in year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		0.8		    vs 10.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.9		    vs 2.9</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 4.3		    vs 4.3</p>
<p> Pretax		     8.6		    vs 28.6</p>
<p> Pretax preexcept	 22.1		   vs 28.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   383.9		  vs 380.4</p>
<p>NOTE - TLG Plc results include an exceptional provision of 13.5 million stg which will be used to rationalise its European fluorescent light fittings manufacturing capacity through the planned closure of its factory in Germany. It also plans to close other smaller manufacturing activities in Europe and Australia.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
